WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.125 --> 00:00:02.782
- [Narrator] Like a scene out of Frozen,

00:00:02.782 --> 00:00:05.856
in the mountains of Shanxi
Province, in Northern China

00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:08.644
lie the Luyashan Mountain's
Ningwu ice caves,

00:00:08.644 --> 00:00:13.585
a spectacle of icicles, ice
falls and ice stalagmites.

00:00:13.585 --> 00:00:16.659
(energetic music)

00:00:16.659 --> 00:00:18.067
These caves are thought to have formed

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:21.886
around three million years
ago, during an early ice age.

00:00:21.886 --> 00:00:24.580
And while there are many caves
like this around the world,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.798
the Ningwu caves are special
for one particular reason.

00:00:28.798 --> 00:00:31.881
This cave stays frozen all year long.

00:00:32.831 --> 00:00:35.729
While temperatures can reach
up to 70 degrees outside

00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:37.583
in the summer, the temperature inside

00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:40.791
never rises above 32 degrees.

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.292
Scientists believe this is due

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:44.822
to the cave's natural bowling pin shape,

00:00:44.822 --> 00:00:47.155
which traps cold air inside.

00:00:49.278 --> 00:00:51.277
Stretching thousands of feet down,

00:00:51.277 --> 00:00:54.108
the top 300 feet are open to the public,

00:00:54.108 --> 00:00:57.547
with five layers connected by
a winding maze of ice stairs,

00:00:57.547 --> 00:00:59.130
holes and bridges.

00:01:01.866 --> 00:01:04.884
Established as a national park in 2005,

00:01:04.884 --> 00:01:07.148
the caves are staged with colorful lights

00:01:07.148 --> 00:01:10.330
emphasizing the grandness
of this ancient cavern.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.830
It is truly a sight to behold.

